n church in Kars, eastern Turkey, built by King Abas I of Bagratid Armenia between about 930 and 943.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-holy-sepulchre"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/church-of-the-holy-sepulchre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Church of the Holy Sepulchre</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Church of the Holy Sepulchre in the Old City of Jerusalem stands on the site that Christian tradition holds to be the place of Jesus's crucifixion and burial.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-holy-spirit-heidelberg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/church-of-the-holy-spirit-heidelberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Church of the Holy Spirit, Heidelberg</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Church of the Holy Spirit is the main church of Heidelberg's old town, built in Gothic style from 1398 and the burial place of several electors palatine.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-holy-spirit-tallinn"><span class="enc-name">Church of the Holy Spirit, Tallinn</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Church of the Holy Spirit is a medieval Gothic church in the old town of Tallinn (Reval), built in the 14th century as the chapel of the town hall and the almshouse.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-intercession-on-the-nerl"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/church-of-the-intercession-on-the-nerl.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Church of the Intercession on the Nerl</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Church of the Intercession on the Nerl is a white-stone church near Bogolyubovo, outside Vladimir in Russia, built in 1165 under Andrei Bogolyubsky.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-society-of-jesus-quito"><span class="enc-name">Church of the Society of Jesus, Quito</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Church of the Society of Jesus, known as La Compañía, is a Jesuit church in the historic centre of Quito, Ecuador, built from 1605 to 1765.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-transfiguration-on-ilyina-street"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/church-of-the-transfiguration-on-ilyina-street.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Church of the Transfiguration on Ilyina Street</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Church of the Transfiguration on Ilyina Street is a medieval church on the Trade Side of Veliky Novgorod, Russia, built in 1374.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/chuson-ji"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/chuson-ji.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Chūson-ji</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Chūson-ji is a Tendai Buddhist temple complex at Hiraizumi in Iwate prefecture, northern Japan.</span></a></li></ul>
